{# One publication, as a card.

   Two callers render the same object and used to carry two copies of this
   markup: the archive listing and the `post` zone of a content grid. They had
   drifted apart by a padding and a hover state, and every improvement had to
   be made twice or made once and forgotten. One file, one card.

   Expects `post` (a listing payload) and `locale`. `terms` is optional - the
   grid zone's payload has none - so it is read defensively rather than
   assumed, `strict_variables` being on.

   `relative` on the article is what the title link's `::after` stretches
   against: the click target is the whole card, while the link itself wraps
   nothing but the title. Wrapping the entire <article> in an <a> would be
   shorter and worse - a screen reader announces a link by its content, so its
   name would become the image, the title and the summary run together in one
   breath.

   `not-prose` because the grid renders inside `<article class="prose">`, and
   Typography would otherwise give the card image `margin: 2em 0`. #}

{# `variant` is optional: a caller that says nothing gets the full card,
   which is what every caller wanted before densities existed.

   - `full`       picture, eyebrow, title, summary, arrow
   - `compact`    a line and an arrow, for a long list in a narrow column
   - `horizontal` the picture beside the text rather than above it #}
{% set variant = variant|default('full') %}

{% set cardTerms = post.terms is defined ? post.terms : [] %}
{% set eyebrow = cardTerms is not empty ? (cardTerms|first)|first : null %}

<article class="group not-prose relative flex h-full overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface transition duration-200 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-highlight-500/60 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-black/30 {{ variant == 'horizontal' ? 'flex-row items-stretch' : 'flex-col' }}">
    {% if post.thumbnailUrl and variant != 'compact' %}
        {# The fit arrives as a class, not a value: Tailwind only emits classes
           it can read in the source, and `object-{{ fit }}` is one it never
           sees. A fixed ratio rather than a fixed height, so a row of cards
           lines up whatever the pictures were. #}
        <div class="relative overflow-hidden {{ variant == 'horizontal' ? 'w-1/3 shrink-0' : '' }}">
            <img
                src="{{ post.thumbnailUrl }}"
                alt=""
                loading="lazy"
                class="{{ variant == 'horizontal' ? 'h-full' : 'aspect-[16/10]' }} w-full {{ post.thumbnailFitClass }} transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"
                style="object-position: {{ post.thumbnailFocalPosition }};"
            >
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col gap-2 {{ variant == 'compact' ? 'p-4' : 'p-5' }}">
        {% if eyebrow and variant != 'compact' %}
            {# The first term, above the title rather than as a chip below it.
               It says what kind of thing this is before the reader commits to
               the title, which is the job a category has on a card. #}
            <p class="m-0 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-highlight">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
        {% endif %}

        {# h2: on a listing these are the sections of the page, and in a grid
           the page's h1 is its own title or its banner's. #}
        <h2 class="m-0 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-primary">
            <a
                href="{{ path('editorial_post', {locale: locale, postTypeSlug: post.postTypeSlug, slug: post.slug}) }}"
                class="no-underline transition-colors group-hover:text-highlight after:absolute after:inset-0"
            >{{ post.title }}</a>
        </h2>

        {% if post.description and variant != 'compact' %}
            <p class="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">{{ post.description }}</p>
        {% endif %}

        {# The affordance the card was missing: nothing here said it could be
           clicked. Hidden from assistive technology because the link above
           already carries the destination, and reserved space rather than
           inserted on hover, so the card does not resize under the cursor. #}
        <span
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="text-lg leading-none text-highlight opacity-0 transition duration-200 group-hover:translate-x-1 group-hover:opacity-100 {{ variant == 'compact' ? 'absolute right-4 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2' : 'mt-auto pt-3' }}"
        >&rarr;</span>
    </div>
</article>
